course: dictionary
lesson: 9987
title: Technically
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Technically is a word for exact rules. It tells you that something is true by the strict meaning of a rule or fact, even when everyday life seems to say otherwise. «Technically, a tomato is a fruit» is true by the exact rules, even though we cook it like a vegetable.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Saying something technically true to hide the truth is still a kind of trick.» The words hide the truth and trick tell you that technically true does not mean honest. The speaker uses the exact words to mislead people.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «according to the exact rules» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Technically can also describe skill, as in «technically brilliant», so always look at the words around it.
fact: Technically means according to the exact rules or facts, even if everyday life seems different.
fact: Technically can also mean relating to skill or method, as in «technically brilliant».
fact: Technically can mean connected with machines, science or technology.
fact: In science, a strict definition is used: technically, a spider is not an insect.
fact: Useful phrases are technically speaking, technically correct and technically possible.
exercise: «Technically, a tomato is a fruit.» What does technically mean here? | *According to the exact rules or facts | Only in a kitchen | In a rude or unfriendly way | Very quickly
exercise: «Her dance was technically brilliant.» What does technically suggest? | Dancing with machines only | Dancing in a rush | Sad and tired | *Great skill and good method
exercise: «Saying something technically true to hide the truth is still a kind of trick.» What does this sentence warn you about? | Technically true words are always the whole truth | Tricks are always against the law | Saying true words is always wrong | *Using true words to hide the truth can still be a trick
test: «A spider is not an insect, technically.» In this sentence, technically means using which idea? | In a robot's way | *The strict scientific definition of an insect | Quickly and carefully | Happily, with a smile
test: Which phrase means the same as «according to the strict rules»? | Very happily | In the rain | *Technically speaking | Once upon a time
exam: Ella says, «Technically you didn't break the rule.» What is the best check to see whether her word fits? | Count the letters in the word | Look for the word happy nearby | *Swap in «according to the exact rules» and see if the sentence still makes sense | Ask if it rhymes with another word
